standard.answer:
The function that prepares and packages the application for deployment is invoked in the `prepare` function located in `src/deploy/functions/prepare.ts`. Specifically, it calls `prepareFunctionsUpload` to package the source directory for each codebase that is being deployed. This is done in the following section of the `prepare` function:

```typescript
if (backend.someEndpoint(wantBackend, (e) => e.platform === "gcfv2")) {
    const packagedSource = await prepareFunctionsUpload(sourceDir, localCfg);
    source.functionsSourceV2 = packagedSource?.pathToSource;
    source.functionsSourceV2Hash = packagedSource?.hash;
}
if (backend.someEndpoint(wantBackend, (e) => e.platform === "gcfv1")) {
    const packagedSource = await prepareFunctionsUpload(sourceDir, localCfg, runtimeConfig);
    source.functionsSourceV1 = packagedSource?.pathToSource;
    source.functionsSourceV1Hash = packagedSource?.hash;
}
```

This indicates that `prepareFunctionsUpload` is called to handle the packaging of the source directory for both GCFv1 and GCFv2 platforms during the deployment process.

